From 88ae043b934be45ef03506ea287b246664eb173c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sfxnz <sfxnz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 12:40:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] inkling2: add vocab-pruned FP8 draft head and wire
 --drafter-bits 4 NVFP4 draft layers

Implement Lever 8a and Lever 8b (target-lossless) for Inkling-2-Mini DFlash2:

- Vocab-pruned draft head (TF_INKLING2_DRAFT_VOCAB, default 0 = full 200,058):
  - Verified Inkling-2-Mini tokenizer.json layout: 199,998 BPE tokens ordered by
    merge rank (0..199997) plus 60 added special tokens at 199998..200057
    (including EOS, thinking, chat, and tool tokens).
  - Pack top K - 60 BPE rows + 60 special tail rows into a compact FP8 (or FP4)
    draft head (tf_ink2_draft_pack_fp8_pruned / tf_ink2_draft_pack_fp4_matrix),
    run topkRows over K rows, and remap local candidate IDs back to global token
    IDs inside tf_ink2_df_select[8]_batch before codebook lookup and Gumbel race.
  - Exact VRAM accounting in draft_fp8.Options.baseBytes -> cuda_capacity.

- Wire up --drafter-bits 4 NVFP4 draft layers (TF_INKLING2_DRAFT_LAYER_BITS=4|8):
  - Add drafter_bits to cuda_native.Options, cuda_mini_capacity.Query, and
    cuda_capacity.Checkpoint.read so CLI --drafter-bits 4|8|0 flows through both
    admission planning (pg.ready_bytes) and weight loading with byte-exact match.
  - Pack the 5 heavy DFlash2 transformer layers (qkv, out, gate_up, down) and fc
    in NVFP4 (qmmf::Mode::fp4 via tf_ink2_draft_pack_fp4_matrix, ~208 MB vs
    ~393 MB FP8G64) while keeping small conv/selector projections in FP8G64.
  - Support Matrix.afterRows() for NVFP4 qkv -> kv suffix slicing and include
    layer precision + draft_vocab in loop_backend warmCacheKey.

Credits (for NOTICE, Apache-2.0 / MIT):
- Draft FP8/FP4 packing framework builds on MiaAI-Lab patch 0006 (commit 9e3cf20b)
  and TensorFold upstream nvfp4q.cuh / qmmf.cu.
